server, ntdll: Run requests directly in the in-process server.

A client thread runs its own request handler under one lock shared with
the server thread, which drops it while it sleeps in kevent, instead of
writing the request to a pipe, waking the server thread and blocking on
the reply. Waits that block still sleep on the wait pipe. Server calls
from a signal handler keep the pipes. The server thread runs at the
user-interactive QoS, and the request census has its own switch
(KITSUNE_SERVER_CENSUS). KITSUNE_SERVER_PIPES=1 turns direct calls off.
---
